<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kabah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kabah is a Maya archaeological site in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puuc">Puuc</a> hills of Yucatán, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, about 20 km south-east of Uxmal, to which it was linked by a raised causeway (sacbe) ending in a free-standing arch. It flourished in the 9th and 10th centuries. Its best-known building, the Codz Poop, has a façade covered with several hundred stone masks of the long-nosed rain god.</p></div>
